Interview                     NannyMUD Times                     Page 4 
 
  We're here with the wizard Cheri today, welcome to the NannyMUD
  Times...
  
  Cheri says: Oh, wait. We're in the void. Come to my workroom.
  
  Q: What's your player's age?
  
  A: I'm an old-timer - I'm 98 days old!
  
  Q: When did you start playing NannyMUD?
  
  A: Oh, ages ago, back in 1997 or so.
  
  Q: What guild did you start in?
  
  A: Knights :)
  
  Q: Were you a knight when you wizzed?
  
  A: Yes, i was an RT. i was actually an RT for about 3 years, then I
     wizzed. :)
     
  Q: How long ago did you wiz?
  
  A: Well, about three years after I started playing.
     Although, I didn't become an RT for about 6 months, so these
     dates are approximate. I'm so old now, my memory is going. ;)
  
  Q: Are you going to create an area?
  
  A: Yes :D I am creating one right now, as a matter of fact. :)
     It's a tremendous amount of work. people have no idea just how much
     work goes into it.
  
  Q: Can you tell us what it is going to be like?
  
  A: Well, the first rooms I will open will sort of pertain to the
     season. There will be tons of stuff to do there like lots of 
     puzzles, a bunch of monsters to kill, etc.
     It will be really great for people who like to explore, as well as
     people who like to kill.
     I hope to expand soon after the first part is approved.
     But, we're not supposed to say that, in case we never finish the
     area, I suppose ;)
  
  Q: How long have you been working on your area, and when do you think it
     will be opened?
  
  A: Well, I hope it will be open right around Christmas time. I started
     this area years ago, but never really learned how to code properly.
     I learned code from lots of different people and became very
     confused. Then, Nothel saved me and took me under his wing.
     Nothel helped me a great deal, but then I quit playing the mud and
     got into making 3d artwork. So, when I came back to Nanny, about 
     2 years ago, I forgot how to code again :(
     I tried to teach myself, and Snafu and Moonchild helped me, too.
     But, it was just too big of a job for them, I think. Moonchild
     suggested that I ask Gemfibrozil to be my sponsor and I was 
     extremely lucky to get her :)
  
  A: I have basically had to recode everything, but I am learning tons
     Gemfibrozil is very detail oriented, and so am I. This means that 
     sometimes our coding sessions end in drinking tequila. ;)
     But, I'm comfortable that the coding is correct and thorough.
  
  Q: Tequila and coding? Sounds like a great combination!
  
  A: Well, honestly, sometimes my brain starts going in loops
     You can't really describe it to someone who has not had experience
     coding. there just are no words.
     I'm a very creative person and the coding part is like pulling
     teeth for me. I have tons of ideas, and fortunately Gemfibrozil 
     is helping me realize them. Plus, we get along great, too :)
  
  Q: Do you still play mortal chars?
  
  A: Yep, but i'm not tellin' ;)
     I have only one mortal.
     I used to have some others long ago, but they were deleted
  
  A: The area I have in mind will be quite large.
     I mean, it's already mostly written.
     Rooms have been created, etc., now they just have to be recoded and
     reworked. That is what is so hard about it, every detail must be 
     paid attention to.
     All in all, it should be a rich area. I hope people like it
  
  Q: Where will it be located?
  
  A: That's what I'm trying to figure out. I'm thinking of that area
     that starts at the foot of the mountains, sort of near Drechbrel's
     area and Mami's area. You know what I mean?
  
  Q: So, it will be a mountainous outdoor setting?
  
  A: Well, it will be both. There are outdoor and indoor settings at 
     first with much more to come ;)
     Mostly what I want to do is have the place come alive.
     I want the players to really feel like they're there :)
     As I grow as a coder, I will hopefully be able to create more and
     more complex monsters and areas.
  
  Q: Do you have any ideas on how to get more players into the MUD?
  
  A: Well, if we make fun areas that are fun to play in, that would
     attract people, I would think. People talk about how they likes 
     games with graphics more than text games, but I disagree.
     It's like when you read a book, then see the movie: the movie is
     *never* as good as the book, because it can never reproduce what is
     in your own imagination.
  
  Q: Do you think NannyMUD needs to be more newbie friendly?
  
  A: Don't you think it is newbie friendly now?
     Cheri laughs.
     I remember my first experience on this mud, lol.
     I was trying to have a conversation with one of the NPCs, lol and
     was really frustrated that it wasn't answering me.
     I figured out how to shout, and shouted for help and no one would
     help, some people just shouted back insults and stuff.
     Finally, a character named Terin took me under his wing and showed
     me the ropes. He was the one who really got me into this game
  
  Q: Any final comments for our readers?
  
  A: I have to say that I really love Nanny.
     I love Nanny and I want to give back for all of the fun I have had
     playing it. That was my motivation for creating an area in the 
     first place. I think the admins have done a tremendous service to 
     us players. They have created an environment that truly brings 
     people together, and that's what it's all about, isn't it?
     I mean, i've never heard of any other game where people actually
     end up marrying each other.
     I hope it stays around a long, long time. and I want to be part of
     it. :)

